From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:45:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: skip the start-up OCV with
 a charger attached

The start-up OCV is the PMIC's battery sample at power-on, taken before
the system loads the battery. With a charger attached it is not a rested
voltage. A power-on while charging samples the charge current's rise and
read 35 % for a cell at about 10 %. A power-on seconds after a cut under
load, cable plugged in to recover, sampled a cell still pulled down and
read 1 %, 15 points under the 16 % of the three boots before. UPower
then took the 1 % for a critical level and powered the system off.

Use the sample only when the PMIC's charger detection reads no charger
at probe. Otherwise take the first OCV reading from the counter window,
as before; on a charger the steady charge current keeps that close, and
the taper and finished-charge readings correct it.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index 3bfcb23..331d175 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@
 #define MT6351_AUXADC_ADC21		0x0e2a
 #define MT6351_PWRON_RDY		BIT(15)
 #define MT6351_PWRON_CODE		GENMASK(14, 0)
+/* The PMIC's charger detection, live. */
+#define MT6351_CHR_CON0			0x0f78
+#define MT6351_RGS_CHRDET		BIT(5)
 #define MT6351_PWRON_MIN_UV		3000000
 #define MT6351_PWRON_MAX_UV		4450000
 /* The software read controls in CON0's upper byte; the lower byte is left. */
@@ -995,13 +998,20 @@ static const enum power_supply_property mt6351_fg_props[] = {
  * start-up, before the system loaded the battery: as the vendor stack does,
  * rather than a voltage and a current taken under the boot's changing load.
  * After a charge, surface charge raises it a few points, which the next rest
- * or charge corrects. Called once at probe.
+ * or charge corrects. With a charger attached the sample carries the charge
+ * current, or follows a cut under load that the charger was plugged in to
+ * recover from, and reads too high or too low, so it is not used then. Called
+ * once at probe.
  */
 static void mt6351_fg_pwron_anchor(struct mt6351_fg *fg)
 {
 	unsigned int val;
 	int uv, mc, pct;
 
+	if (regmap_read(fg->regmap, MT6351_CHR_CON0, &val) || (val & MT6351_RGS_CHRDET)) {
+		dev_info(fg->dev, "charger present: start-up OCV not used\n");
+		return;
+	}
 	if (regmap_read(fg->regmap, MT6351_AUXADC_ADC21, &val) ||
 	    !(val & MT6351_PWRON_RDY) || thermal_zone_get_temp(fg->tz, &mc))
 		return;
